GED - Golang ed.
its a like ed but in go.
i just made it why not.

For compile source code just use "go build ." and after run by "./ged" command.

-- EXAMPLES FOR INPUT OF THE EDITOR -- 
Input:
binary|html|hello world|html|binary

Output:
\x3c\x68\x31\x3e\x68\x68|\x6c\x6c\x6f\x20\x77\x6f\x72\x6c\x64\x3c\x2f\x68\x31\x3e


-- EXAMPLES OF KEYWORDS -- 

binary: set binary mode, will convert text to binary

html: set html mode, will convert text to html

write: write current text to file

quit: quit the program

remove <NUMBER>: removes last symbols in the text.

and a '|' is used to separate commands, so you can use multiple commands at once.

if you use tags such as "html" and "binary" again, its turn off text convert, so "html|hello|html|hello" will write "<h1>hello</h1>hello".